From: Pietro Ameruoso <p.ameruoso@live.it>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 00:08:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: as21xxx: handle stale IDs during driver matching

The AS21xxx can return the response from the preceding Clause 45
transaction. The PHY-ID reads performed by match_phy_device() happen before
a model-specific driver is bound, so they cannot use the driver's read_mmd
workaround. A stale IPC or PHY-ID response can therefore prevent the
model-specific driver from matching.

Reuse as21xxx_read_mmd() for the match-time PHY-ID reads. It cannot be
reached through phy_read_mmd() at this stage because phydev->drv has not
been assigned yet.

The initial Clause 45 scan can also cache a PCS ID of 0xffffffff when the
PHY does not answer before its firmware-described reset sequence completes.
Phylib applies that reset before driver matching, but the AS21xxx matcher
rejects the stale cached ID before reading the live model ID.

When the cached PCS ID is invalid, refresh it in the AS21xxx matcher using
the delayed-read workaround. This keeps both workarounds local to the
affected PHY family and allows normal vendor and model matching after reset
deassertion.

Signed-off-by: Pietro Ameruoso <p.ameruoso@live.it>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
@@ -900,6 +900,32 @@ static int as21xxx_led_polarity_set(stru
 			      mask, val);
 }
 
+/* phydev->drv is not assigned while match_phy_device() is running, so
+ * phy_read_mmd() cannot dispatch to the AS21xxx read workaround.
+ */
+static int as21xxx_read_mmd(struct phy_device *phydev, int devad,
+			    u16 regnum);
+
+static int as21xxx_match_refresh_pcs_id(struct phy_device *phydev)
+{
+	u32 phy_id;
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = as21xxx_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PCS, MII_PHYSID1);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+	phy_id = ret << 16;
+
+	ret = as21xxx_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PCS, MII_PHYSID2);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+	phy_id |= ret;
+
+	phydev->c45_ids.device_ids[MDIO_MMD_PCS] = phy_id;
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int as21xxx_match_phy_device(struct phy_device *phydev,
 				    const struct phy_driver *phydrv)
 {
@@ -908,18 +934,24 @@ static int as21xxx_match_phy_device(stru
 	u32 phy_id;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (phydev->c45_ids.device_ids[MDIO_MMD_PCS] == 0xffffffff) {
+		ret = as21xxx_match_refresh_pcs_id(phydev);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	/* Skip PHY that are not AS21xxx */
 	if (!phy_id_compare_vendor(phydev->c45_ids.device_ids[MDIO_MMD_PCS],
 				   PHY_VENDOR_AEONSEMI))
 		return genphy_match_phy_device(phydev, phydrv);
 
 	/* Read PHY ID to handle firmware loaded or HW reset */
-	ret = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PCS, MII_PHYSID1);
+	ret = as21xxx_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PCS, MII_PHYSID1);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 	phy_id = ret << 16;
 
-	ret = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PCS, MII_PHYSID2);
+	ret = as21xxx_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_PCS, MII_PHYSID2);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 	phy_id |= ret;

